    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// Four-on-the-floor with a pushed bass (docs/prompts/69)." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// Every part here is written on the grid, because that is what the grid is" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// for. What makes it move is that the bass's offbeat eighths land a" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// sixty-fourth early — the anticipation of house and garage, and a thing no" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// notation has an element for. It is a groove, so it is written once in the" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// profile and nowhere on the page." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The kick does *not* push. That asymmetry is the piece: a groove is per" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// part, because the whole effect is one part disagreeing with another on" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// purpose." },
